# Keep the build context small. Without this, `COPY . .` ships the whole
# target/ directory (multiple GB) into the daemon on every build, and `fly
# deploy` uploads it over the network before anything is compiled.
#
# The image builds from source, so it needs Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock, src/,
# static/, migrations/ and nothing else.

# Build artifacts — by far the largest offender.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local state that must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# VCS and CI metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.editorconfig
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Docs and repo furniture: irrelevant to the binary, and changing a README
# should not invalidate the Docker layer cache.
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
docker-compose.yml
deny.toml
openapi.yaml
redocly.yaml
fly.toml
